 Assess stakeholder feedback, engagement outcomes, and resistance indicators, recommending actions to improve adoption and address risks; 
 Facilitate consultations, workshops, focus groups, town halls, and other engagement activities to support alignment and commitment to change objectives; 
 Coordinate the identification of learning and capability needs arising from change impacts and support the development and evaluation of training plans; 
 Coordinate organizational readiness and go-live activities, including readiness assessments, evidence collection, issue follow-up, and escalation of unresolved concerns; 
 Support post-implementation stabilization and sustainment activities by monitoring adoption, identifying support needs, and tracking lessons learned; 
 Develop and coordinate change communications and engagement materials, ensuring messaging aligns with the SIS change strategy and institutional communication standards; 
 Translate technical and project information into clear, audience-appropriate communications, presentations, and stakeholder resources; 
 Maintain the SIS communications calendar and coordinate content development, approvals, publication, and distribution. 
